			<div class="content" id="post-content-4182183">
									

<p>I just can't take this seriously as a mainlist article. It's way too goofy while also trying to be self-serious and the text alterations feel over-the-top ridiculous. Were this a -J it would be amusing but as it stands I can't take this seriously as written.</p>
<p>The concept of the people in a geographic area losing their sense of right and wrong isn't explained very well and the sentence &quot;People within this area no longer conceptualize the belief that crime is something which should be stopped&quot; feels like it's begging for greater depth in its criteria for how different people perceive crime.</p>
<p>I also don't think it was well-explained why losing the sense of criminal consequences would lead people to riot. Is it a statement on the human condition, or is the escalation also a part of the anomalous effect?</p>
<p>The Archon psuedo-object class feels more like an excuse to skip out on the special containment procedures than something which adds anything to the narrative.</p>
<p>Also, the think that I think drags this down more than anything is that the Spectre is just not an interesting character as presented here. He's very one-dimensional.</p>
<p>-1</p>

